WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.452
Exercise 7: CI/CD with GitHub Actions in your own fork.

2
00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:09.453
The pipeline runs three checks: syntax, reality, and compatibility.

3
00:00:09.504 --> 00:00:21.499
Remove the exercise files from .gitignore, then commit and push them to your fork.

4
00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:29.572
Create the workflow. First: install the pinned CLIs and lint all files.

5
00:00:29.622 --> 00:00:34.074
Lint checks the syntax against the ODCS and ODPS standards.

6
00:00:34.123 --> 00:00:43.066
Then test against reality: start the database, create the views, run datacontract ci.

7
00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:50.976
Break the lint on purpose: logicalType text is not ODCS. This is what the run reports.

8
00:00:51.025 --> 00:01:00.528
Break a type: the test against the database finds bigint, not integer.

9
00:01:00.578 --> 00:01:08.033
Push: GitHub Actions runs the workflow on every change to main.

10
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:16.536
datacontract ci writes a step summary: every contract, every check.

11
00:01:16.586 --> 00:01:26.297
Before the third check, try datacontract breaking locally. v1 to v2 adds a field: no error.

12
00:01:26.347 --> 00:01:37.493
The other way round removes quantity: ERROR and exit code 1.

13
00:01:37.543 --> 00:01:44.957
On pull requests, compare every contract with its version on the base branch.

14
00:01:45.007 --> 00:01:49.959
A breaking change makes the job fail.

15
00:01:50.009 --> 00:02:01.592
Try it: remove customer_id on a branch, push it, and open a pull request in your fork.

16
00:02:01.642 --> 00:02:09.594
The Breaking changes check fails. Lint and test still pass.

17
00:02:09.644 --> 00:02:17.596
The log says why: customer_id was removed. That would break consumers.

18
00:02:17.647 --> 00:02:25.097
Make a compatible change instead, or release a new major version. Tip: require the check with branch protection.
